  <section id="faq" data-screen-label="FAQ" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);">
    <div style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(56px,8vw,88px) 28px">
      <div style="font:500 12px var(--font-mono);color:#A8FF45;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:18px">/ FAQ</div>
      <h2 style="font:600 var(--type-display-2)/1.08 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 40px;color:#A8FF45;text-wrap:balance">Common questions</h2>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:28px 40px">
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Which chains do you cover?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">EVM chains primarily: Ethereum, Base, Arbitrum, Optimism, Polygon, and BNB Chain. Ask about non-EVM and we will be straight about our depth rather than take the work.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Is SolidityScan separate from CredShields?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">SolidityScan is our scanner and keeps its own name because it has its own market. Same company, same audit team behind it.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Do we need an audit if we scanned already?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Scanning covers known patterns and regressions across every commit. An audit tests your specific protocol economics, which no scanner can anticipate. Most teams need both.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Can you test the application around our contracts?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Yes, and it is where most real losses start. Contract audits and application testing come from the same company, which is unusual in this space.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Do you publish audit reports?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Only if you want them published. Many clients publish the contract audit for community trust and keep the application report private.</p>
        </div>
